\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {23}{\ignorespaces Covariant Navier--Stokes specialization audit. Raw physical expenditure obeys \(p=r(D+M)\); it is admitted as target price only by the local target-aligned carrier graph. The collapsing branch is followed by the parabolic microscope. The induced scale and translation currents enter the exact signed carrier identity. Compatible cells are glued before positive parts are taken. The shell covector then generates the adjoint-linearized cyclic module, Reynolds and pressure defects, commutator productions, and their joint kernel. Strict carrier deficit excludes an infinite chain, while equality restricts the zero-production kernel and reruns prospective selection. The aggregate feeding class is evaluated before its support is disintegrated: a nonzero class returns its support as the next successor, whereas the zero class forces the record-scale production kernel and removes the target. Every total-graph failure retains the complete active signature in its source-typed successor cell.}}{172}{figure.23}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ns-backend-audit}{{23}{172}{Covariant Navier--Stokes specialization audit. Raw physical expenditure obeys \(p=r(D+M)\); it is admitted as target price only by the local target-aligned carrier graph. The collapsing branch is followed by the parabolic microscope. The induced scale and translation currents enter the exact signed carrier identity. Compatible cells are glued before positive parts are taken. The shell covector then generates the adjoint-linearized cyclic module, Reynolds and pressure defects, commutator productions, and their joint kernel. Strict carrier deficit excludes an infinite chain, while equality restricts the zero-production kernel and reruns prospective selection. The aggregate feeding class is evaluated before its support is disintegrated: a nonzero class returns its support as the next successor, whereas the zero class forces the record-scale production kernel and removes the target. Every total-graph failure retains the complete active signature in its source-typed successor cell}{figure.23}{}}
\newlabel{fig:ns-backend-audit@cref}{{[figure][23][]23}{[1][171][]172}{}{}{}}
